# .dockerignore for the WIDENED fold build context (spec 012 S9a).
#
# Copy this file to the ROOT of the context directory — the parent that
# holds r5e-enterprise/, r5e-kernel/ and r5e-core/ side by side — as
# `.dockerignore`. The legacy builder reads only that one file; a
# per-Dockerfile `Dockerfile.fold.dockerignore` needs BuildKit, which the
# quickstart does not assume (Dockerfile header). Paths are relative to
# the context root.
#
# Everything is excluded, then the three trees the build needs are let
# back in, minus their build artifacts, state, secrets and VCS metadata.
# This is the public .dockerignore under an `r5e-enterprise/` prefix, with
# one deliberate difference: apps/recurse_fold/ is IN.
#
# R4-F6 (RC review 2026-09-05): what is excluded here is **artifacts and
# state only**, never tracked source. The build now recomputes the three
# `archiveSha256` values in `repos.lock.json` from the context itself
# (`scripts/verify-source-archive.py`, the `verify-sources` stage in the
# Dockerfile), so the manifest is a check rather than a label — and that
# check can only pass if the context carries exactly the trees the
# manifest hashes. Excluding `docs/`, `specs/`, `.specify/` or the
# kernel's `test/` here would make every build fail with three mismatched
# hashes. When the context is a frozen release context (the ordinary
# case) it *is* the extracted archive and holds none of the artifacts
# below; the exclusions below matter for a widened context over live
# checkouts, where they keep `_build`, `deps` and keys out.

*
!r5e-enterprise
!r5e-kernel
!r5e-core
!r5e-core/verifier
!r5e-core/LICENSE
!r5e-core/LICENSE.md
!repos.lock.json

# --- r5e-enterprise: the public .dockerignore, prefixed -----------------
r5e-enterprise/_build
r5e-enterprise/deps
r5e-enterprise/cover
r5e-enterprise/doc
r5e-enterprise/**/*.beam
r5e-enterprise/**/erl_crash.dump
r5e-enterprise/.git
r5e-enterprise/.jj
r5e-enterprise/.env
r5e-enterprise/.env.*
# `.env.example` is tracked, published, and part of the hashed tree.
!r5e-enterprise/.env.example
r5e-enterprise/**/*.pem
r5e-enterprise/**/*.key
r5e-enterprise/secrets
r5e-enterprise/.envrc
r5e-enterprise/.envrc.local
r5e-enterprise/**/*.log
r5e-enterprise/.giulia
r5e-enterprise/.r5e
# `.claude/` and `.codex/` are agent working state and are excluded from
# the public tree by `scripts/prepare-release.py`, so a release context
# never carries them; the lines stay for the live-checkout case.
r5e-enterprise/.claude
r5e-enterprise/.codex
r5e-enterprise/local-gan-runs
r5e-enterprise/tmp-gan
r5e-enterprise/**/__pycache__
r5e-enterprise/native/*/target
r5e-enterprise/node_modules
r5e-enterprise/ui/node_modules
r5e-enterprise/ui/dist
r5e-enterprise/ui/.vite
r5e-enterprise/ui/coverage
r5e-enterprise/ui/playwright-report
r5e-enterprise/ui/test-results
# The fold's own throwaway kernel state (dev / demo runs).
r5e-enterprise/apps/recurse_fold/.r5e-*
r5e-enterprise/apps/recurse_fold/fold-demo-verification.txt
# --- r5e-kernel ---------------------------------------------------------
r5e-kernel/_build
r5e-kernel/deps
r5e-kernel/.git
r5e-kernel/.jj
# Every kernel data dir, the live genesis chain first among them.
r5e-kernel/.r5e
r5e-kernel/.r5e.*
r5e-kernel/.r5e-*
r5e-kernel/erl_crash.dump

# --- r5e-core/verifier --------------------------------------------------
r5e-core/verifier/_build
r5e-core/verifier/deps
r5e-core/verifier/recurse_verify
r5e-core/verifier/erl_crash.dump
